    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0094" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-18">December 18,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have your letter of
                    December eighteenth relative to the important question of a meeting with the
                    British and the Dutch concerning raw materials.</p>
                <pb facs="0095" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/>
                <p>In accord with your request I am glad to assign Mr. Thomas K. Finletter as a
                    member of the group and have advised him accordingly.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
